          "why_it_matters": "Benny Sings earns a RADAR slot less through virtuoso display than through an unusually recognizable sense of pocket and miniature arrangement: soft soul, R&B, pop craft and beat-minded production compressed into songs that sound deceptively easy. This Tokyo return has a real current center because it arrives with 22 Durnham Dew rather than as a catalog stop, and WWW X is a useful scale for hearing whether those tightly built studio grooves open up onstage. The one-night return after three years adds context without turning the show into a scarcity event.",
